# Proposed by the swarm's review (2026-10-14); the documenter may edit or drop it.
# Story: someone works in Safari, framed on its own. Things happen around them:
# only what takes the keyboard moves the camera.
# Reference: T32 T07 T52.
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 101 bottom
zoom 101
# Notes changes its focused window in the background (a reminder fires).
background-focus 102
flush
flush
flush
flush
expect camera 101
expect hidden 102
# A second Safari window opens over the framed one: it stays usable, the camera stays.
open Safari 500x400
expect camera 101
expect visible 104
# Zooming out leaves it exactly where it is: its frame is its person's (Q20).
show-all
expect visible 104
expect at 104 300 200 500x400
# ⌘Tab to a window out of view shows it, and the level is kept: from one framed window to another.
zoom 101
focus 102
expect fills 102
expect hidden 101
back
expect fills 101
# From a group the view steps out just far enough to show both.
out
focus 102
expect visible 101
expect visible 102
# A minimized window clicked in the Dock gets the keyboard while it is still flying out.
# It comes back to its slot; the camera does not zoom onto it.
show-all
minimize 103
focus 103
restore 103
expect camera root
expect above 101 103
# Closing the framed window steps out instead of staring at nothing.
zoom 103
close 103
expect visible 101
# Hiding the framed window's app shows its surroundings; showing it again returns.
zoom 101
hide Safari
expect visible 102
unhide Safari
expect fills 101
